nversation": 120314, "other": 423, "system": 32543, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 104483}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 272160}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "64890bdc-38fe-56a0-8184-5ef857457c6e", "at": 1795626394.7944155, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3010, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "9802b473-1fee-57fe-98ee-cddd06905fa7", "at": 1795626395.7018204, "until": 1795626395.723824, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3011, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (8 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "c0f99243-1bb6-5ed5-8f35-c56f7280fd9b", "at": 1795626395.7261844, "until": 1795626411.8559318, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3019, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01SDQwecYjoxMXRx2SeGb9CX", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q origin main && python3 - <<'EOF' p='Brief.md' s=open(p).read() def rep(a,b): global s assert a in s, a[:40] s=s.replace(a,b) rep(\"# B…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q origin main && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:40]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# Brief — the idea (rev 2, after idea-review 1)\",\"# Brief — the idea (rev 3, after idea-review 1 and its re-review)\")\nrep(\"d ≤ 10: m ∈ {32, 128, 512} (below 2^d−2, so genuinely sampled) plus the default (exact), n ≈ 100, R = 100\",\n    \"d ≤ 10: m ∈ {5%, 15%, 50%} of the 2^d−2 non-trivial coalitions (Pima 13/38/127; d=10: 51/153/511 — sampled for every d), plus the shap default (exact for these d), n ≈ 100, R = 100\")\nrep(\"Per run, m×50 evaluations; budgets are evaluated from nested prefixes of one sample stream so one stream serves all budgets.\",\n    \"Per run, m×50 evaluations. Streams: the paired/unbiased Kernel SHAP and the antithetic permutation estimator draw one sample stream per repeat whose prefixes serve all budgets (nested); shap's default Kernel SHAP enumerates the extreme coalition sizes first and is **not** a prefix of one stream, so each of its budgets is a separate run. Three estimators therefore mean three streams (default: one run per budget). **The 1.4 s figure is a synthetic 100-tree forest (min_samples_leaf=5); the first job of `experiment-repo` is to re-time the actual fitted RF/GBM/MLP on German and ACS, and the table is re-based on that.**\")\nrep(\"| d ≥ 16: ≈ 1.4 s per RF stream of 4096×50 ⇒ 3.6k runs ≈ 1.4 CPU-h per RF cell, ~4–5 CPU-h per dataset over 4 models; d ≤ 10: ≈ 0.2 s per run ⇒ < 1 CPU-h per RF cell, ~2–3 CPU-h per dataset |\",\n    \"| d ≥ 16: ≈ 1.4 s per RF stream of 4096×50 ⇒ 3.6k runs ≈ 1.4 CPU-h per RF cell **per estimator stream** (default Kernel SHAP, paired/unbiased, permutation ⇒ ×3, partly offset by cheaper LR/MLP and by cache reuse), so ~10–12 CPU-h per d ≥ 16 dataset before re-timing, not 4–5; d ≤ 10: ≈ 0.2 s per run ⇒ ~2–3 CPU-h per dataset over all models and estimators |\")\nrep(\"| ≈ 5–6 CPU-h |\",\"| ≈ 5–6 CPU-h for E1/E2 and the floors of RF/GBM/LR; plus German MLP E1 (≈ 5·10^7 evals ≈ 2.5 min per instance × a reduced set of ~30 instances ≈ 1.3 CPU-h) and, for MLPs at d=20, floor (c) with an E3-flagged reference (MLP retrains × high-budget runs; ≈ 1–2 CPU-h) |\")\nrep(\"| Total tier 1 | | ≈ 20–24 CPU-h; thin margin ⇒ cut order below |\",\n    \"| Total tier 1 | | **≈ 30–40 CPU-h at current estimates, over the ~24 h envelope**; so the grid is cut by the order below to fit after re-timing, and the paper states what was cut |\")\nrep(\"Cut order if compute falls short: tier 2 → R and n on non-headline cells → PL (permutation) estimator → low-d datasets down to Pima + one of Income/GMSC.\",\n    \"Cut order if compute falls short: tier 2 → R and n on non-headline cells → permutation estimator on d ≥ 16 datasets → low-d datasets down to Pima + one of Income/GMSC → paired/unbiased stream limited to the cells where the certificate (H4) is tested.\")\nrep(\"Both reported, plus results stratified by exact margin\",\n    \"Both reported, plus the share of instances whose tolerance group is large (more than one feature beyond the boundary pair, i.e. a nearly flat attribution where P_c^ε passes vacuously), and results stratified by exact margin\")\nrep(\"with per-instance intervals\",\"with the (ε = 0.05, 0.9) headline accompanied by its sensitivity grid (ε ∈ {0, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1}, threshold ∈ {0.8, 0.9, 0.95}), per-instance intervals\")\nrep(\"Hierarchical resampling dataset > model > instance; repeats are collapsed to per-instance P_c (and A) first, never treated as independent evidence.\",\n    \"**Per-dataset (and per-model) results are the primary display**, with CIs from resampling instances (and, within a cell, models/retrains); repeats are collapsed to per-instance P_c (and A) first, never treated as independent evidence. A pooled summary across datasets is labelled descriptive and carries **no dataset-level CI** (4–5 clusters cannot support one); whether a pattern holds across\n[truncated for publication]"]], "output": "```console\nhttp://172.17.0.1:44601/world/idea-repo/issues/3#issuecomment-6\nClosed #3\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "deedaa0c-c4c1-58ef-b4b5-8ec88120ef07", "at": 1795626410.9022272, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3021, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "fc0ff9a3-7a87-51ab-8a4e-af1cba918100", "at": 1795626410.9185534, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3022, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "1f6f9c2c-ccef-550f-9879-0c3baaffd138", "at": 1795626410.9228144, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3023, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "3d148d65-b0b4-5c58-86be-9b2c10d6e150", "at": 1795626410.979635, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3024, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "a2ba6a4371a534c1de9bb2a0f9636ca1", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge GET 